      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "New clinical findings demonstrate a high efficacy of clofelin (100-200 mcg epidurally) as a nonopiate analgesic at the pre-, intra-, and postoperative stages of anesthesiologic care. Prospects of using clofelin in combination with morphine are discussed, as is the use of guanfacine as an agent for prolonged analgesia in the postoperative period."},
